he odd numbers from this sequence, sorted in increasing order.\\n- **Edge Cases**:\\n  - If `n` is 1, the output should be `[1]`.\\n  - If `n` is even, the first odd number in the sequence will be `n` itself, if it is odd.\\n  - If the sequence does not contain any odd numbers (which is not possible given the rules), the output should be an empty list."}'}]
